# {{PROJECT_TITLE}}

A full-stack [Bloom](https://github.com/bloomneo/bloom) app: React +
[@bloomneo/uikit](https://github.com/bloomneo/uikit) on the web, Express +
[@bloomneo/appkit](https://github.com/bloomneo/appkit) for the API, with routes
declared once as contracts shared by both.

## Quick start

```bash
npm install
npm run dev          # API on http://localhost:3000, web on http://localhost:5173
```

```bash
npm run typecheck    # web and API
npm run build        # web + API into dist/
npm start            # production server (serves the web build too)
npx bloom check      # every route has an auth decision, every contract is served,
                     # tenant tables have row-level security, versions in step
npx bloom manifest   # after changing a contract: refresh bloom.manifest.json + AGENTS.md
```

`.github/workflows/bloom-check.yml` runs `bloom check` on every push and pull
request.

## Where things are

```
src/
├── contracts/                 # routes declared once (defineRoute), used by web and API
│   └── welcome.contract.ts
├── api/                       # Express + @bloomneo/appkit
│   ├── server.ts              # createApiRouter, frontend key, request ids, /health
│   └── features/<name>/       # <name>.route.ts → mounted automatically
└── web/                       # React + @bloomneo/uikit
    ├── main.tsx               # providers + <PageRouter> from @bloomneo/uikit/router
    ├── pages.ts               # the page glob — the app's only routing code
    ├── features/<name>/pages/ # a file's location is its URL (main → /)
    ├── shared/                # client.ts (contracts), api.ts, layouts, brand
    └── styles/                # brand.css — the colour tokens
```

## Add a page

Create `src/web/features/products/pages/index.tsx` with a default-exported
component. `/products` exists — no route table, no restart.

## Add an API route

1. Declare it in `src/contracts/products.contract.ts`:
   `defineRoute({ method, path: '/api/products', response, auth: 'user' })`.
2. Serve it from `src/api/features/products/products.route.ts`:
   `export default await contractRouter([route(listProducts, ({ user }) => …)])`.
3. Call it from the web: `await client.call(listProducts)`.
4. Run `npx bloom manifest` and `npx bloom check`.

`route()` applies the contract's auth, tenant context and validation; the
handler returns the body.

## Database

SQLite is the zero-setup default (`DATABASE_URL=file:./dev.db`). For
production — and any multi-tenant app — use Postgres with
`BLOOM_DB_TENANT=rls`.

